INT. SAFE-DEPOSIT VAULT, PRIVATE BANK - NIGHT

Rows of brass boxes under a vaulted ceiling. A single green banker's lamp. The air is cold and smells of old metal.

GIDEON ASHWORTH-DEMBELE (50s, impeccable suit, silver cufflinks) stands before an open drawer, fingers curled around a velvet pouch. Facing him, in the narrow aisle, LUCRETIA FONTAINE-OKAFOR (40s, black gloves, revolver steady) blocks his exit.

Gideon turns. Lucretia does not lower the gun.

GIDEON
You're early.

LUCRETIA
You're late.

Gideon smiles and lifts the pouch. Lucretia's eyes drop to it.

GIDEON
^It's not what you think.

LUCRETIA
^It's exactly what I think.

They speak together, flat, certain. A drip falls somewhere in the dark.

GIDEON
Lucretia. Put it down.

LUCRETIA
You first.

He opens his fingers. The pouch lands on the marble with a soft chink. Lucretia exhales, almost relieved, and kicks it toward the wall.

The gun doesn't waver.
